Sable and Suns is a military contractor that goes the extra mile. Where other companies might sell you weapons and vehicles, S&S will send a consultant to teach you how to use them. Technically unaffiliated with the countries of Edan, S&S openly plays all sides. They're one of the major contractors that supply the [[Geography/Calaria/index|Calarian]] military, but [[Org/Protectorate/index|Protectorate]], the Pirate-Kings of [[Geography/Lorandris/index|Lorandris]], and some up-and-coming [[Org/index|Orgs]] out of [[Geography/Rhædon/index|Rhædon]] all hold contracts with them.

When dealing with mercenary gangs and bandits, if their weaponry is of S&S make, that's a telltale sign that someone with money is backing them. Sable and Suns firearms and blades are high quality but don't come cheap.

Four robbers who attacked the Party at a rest-stop gas station outside [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] each carried one of the company's tokens, and the survivor said they had bought their guns from a man named Lark, in a neighborhood of Hallia called [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Deosil|Deosil]].

Over downtime [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] went to a Sable and Suns contact under the name of the [[Org/Ghosts of Raelion|Ghosts]], asking after high-calibre firearms and hinting that the Ghosts were planning something that needed them. The company cannot yet fill that order. It works with a consultant named Salo Murn, who returned from an expedition starward with a little technology taken from a city he had raided, and it is gearing up to send out again to fetch more, the only thing standing between it and larger guns. Until then its salesmen will happily trade up to its older firearms.
